I did not add the enrichment fetch. It needs `aap:caps/http-client`, which the node's `with` clause doesn't grant, and `RunInfo` has no text field to build the query from. Adding the import would break the capability contract, and a fetch to an external host on every call would send data outside the node's authority. If you want enrichment, grant the node an HTTP capability scoped to that host and add a field the query can come from.

Two assumptions in the body: the subscriptions are stored under key `urls` as newline-separated values, and a missing key yields an empty list, which still satisfies `present(urls)` because the field is always present.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = match state_read::get("urls") {
            Some(raw) => raw
                .lines()
                .map(str::trim)
                .filter(|line| !line.is_empty())
                .map(String::from)
                .collect(),
            None => Vec::new(),
        };
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

